    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a productive slate today, headlined by **Drake Baldwin**, who sits at the top of our board with a 70.49 score. Batting leadoff against Sugano, **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and the ideal setup of an optimal batting order. Joining him in the \"Strong\" category is **Coby Mayo** (65.56), who finds a favorable matchup against Lopez, J. **Coby Mayo** gains significant leverage from a 10% park factor bump and an 18% advantage against the opposing starter, making him our anchor at the hot corner. **Heliot Ramos** also clears the 60-point threshold, utilizing a strong platoon edge and order placement to project as a high-floor asset in the outfield.\n\nWhile we are navigating a few \"Marginal\" plays to fill the roster, the most difficult decision was the exclusion of our depth pieces in favor of the current outfield configuration. **Wade Meckler** (51.79) narrowly edged out internal competition for the final outfield slot, as his favorable matchup against Painter offered a higher efficiency floor than our deeper bench options. We remain cautious with **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.98), whose raw talent is capped today by a difficult platoon matchup that dragged his score down 15%. Additionally, owners should note the absence of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, all of whom are unavailable due to rest or IL designations, forcing us to lean heavily on the active core. We are monitoring all lineups closely for late scratches, but as it stands, our focus remains on **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** to drive the offensive output.",
